## Information Obtaining Method and Apparatus

An information obtaining method is provided for enabling a user to access information related to content being browsed with a reduced number of user operations. The method may be performed by a terminal apparatus, a server apparatus, or a distributed system including the terminal apparatus and the server apparatus.

The method comprises: obtaining browsed content displayed or to be displayed by a browsing application; analyzing the browsed content to identify one or more terms satisfying a predetermined relevance condition; determining, for each identified term, related information or a network location from which the related information is obtainable; generating link information associating the identified term with the related information or the network location; and causing the browsed content to be presented such that the identified term includes a user-selectable link.

In response to receiving a selection of the user-selectable link, the method further comprises obtaining the related information and causing the related information to be displayed. Accordingly, the user may access information related to a term appearing in the browsed content without separately entering a search query or navigating through multiple screens.

The browsed content may include, without limitation, a web page, an electronic document, an electronic message, an image containing recognized text, an audio or video transcript, or content presented by an application. Identification of a relevant term may be based on one or more of a term dictionary, semantic analysis, named-entity recognition, contextual similarity, user preference information, browsing history, access frequency, current location, temporal information, or relationships between terms stored in a knowledge database.

The related information may comprise a definition, explanatory information, product information, map information, news information, multimedia content, search results, or information concerning a person, place, organization, event, or subject represented by the identified term. The related information may be displayed in a separate page, a pop-up region, an overlay, an expandable portion of the browsed content, or another presentation area.

An information obtaining apparatus comprises:

- a content obtaining unit configured to obtain content being browsed by a user;
- a term identifying unit configured to identify, from the content, at least one term associated with related information;
- a link determining unit configured to determine a destination or information resource corresponding to the identified term;
- a link adding unit configured to associate a selectable link with the identified term in the browsed content;
- a display control unit configured to cause the content including the selectable link to be displayed; and
- an information obtaining unit configured, in response to selection of the selectable link, to obtain and present the related information.

The link adding unit may modify document data before rendering, modify a document object model after rendering, or generate a display layer superimposed on the browsed content without altering original content data. The apparatus may further include a ranking unit configured to rank candidate terms or candidate information resources and to add a link only when a relevance score satisfies a threshold condition. Duplicate, excessive, or contextually inappropriate links may thereby be suppressed.

In one embodiment, term identification and link insertion are performed by a user terminal. In another embodiment, a server analyzes requested content and transmits link information to the user terminal. In a further embodiment, the terminal identifies candidate terms and the server determines corresponding related information.

By automatically detecting relevant terms and associating the terms with directly selectable information resources, the disclosed method and apparatus reduce the need for text copying, query entry, application switching, and repeated navigation operations.

### Exemplary Independent Method Claim

1. An information obtaining method performed by one or more processors, the method comprising:  
   obtaining content presented for browsing by a user;  
   identifying, from the content, a term satisfying a relevance condition;  
   determining an information resource corresponding to the term;  
   associating, automatically and without receiving a search query directed to the term, a selectable link with an occurrence of the term in the content;  
   causing the content including the selectable link to be displayed; and  
   in response to selection of the selectable link, obtaining information from the information resource and causing the obtained information to be presented.

### Exemplary Independent Apparatus Claim

2. An information obtaining apparatus comprising:  
   one or more processors; and  
   a memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the apparatus to:  
   obtain content being browsed by a user;  
   identify a term included in the content based on a relevance criterion;  
   determine related information corresponding to the identified term;  
   add, to a displayed representation of the content, a selectable link associated with the identified term; and  
   responsive to selection of the selectable link, obtain and present the related information.
